{
  // Which files the documentation linter reads.
  //
  // The exclusions fall into three groups, and the second and third are the
  // interesting ones:
  //
  //  - Build output and dependencies, which nobody wrote prose into.
  //  - `.context/`, which holds the AI's own session memory and the upstream
  //    GPL source. Neither is this project's documentation, and the upstream tree
  //    is not even in git. `.caim` is listed as well because it is a *symlink* to
  //    `.context/ai-memory`: markdownlint matches on the path it walks, which is
  //    `.caim/...`, so excluding `.context` alone would pull 2 MB of session
  //    transcript into the lint and report every "Assistant" heading in it.
  //  - `.agents/`, `.gemini/`, `.opencode/`, `.agent/` and `.github/copilot.md`.
  //    These are symlinks into `.agents/`, so linting them would lint the same
  //    file once per link and report each finding five times.
  //
  // `openspec/changes/` is excluded on purpose too, and it is the one exclusion
  // worth an argument: those are work-in-progress plans whose shape is owned by
  // the OpenSpec tooling, and `tasks.md` in particular is a checklist that reads
  // badly with a linter's spacing rules applied. `openspec/specs/` - the settled
  // specifications, which are a deliverable - is linted.
  "config": ".markdownlint.json",
  "ignores": [
    "**/node_modules/**",
    "**/dist/**",
    "**/coverage/**",
    "**/.git/**",
    "**/.context/**",
    "**/.caim/**",
    "**/.agents/**",
    "**/.agent/**",
    "**/.gemini/**",
    "**/.opencode/**",
    "**/.github/**",
    "**/openspec/changes/**"
  ]
}